# OpenEarth Viewer — Project Overview

Marine data map viewer by Deltares/OpenEarth. Embeddable, multi-tenant: one codebase serves multiple viewer configs (Wadden, WOZE, IHM, etc.) via URL slug and DatoCMS content.

**Live:** https://rws-viewer.netlify.app/

## Tech Stack

- **Vue 2.7** + Vue Router (history mode) + Vuex + Vuetify 2
- **Mapbox GL** via `vue2mapbox-gl`; map layers from WMS and WMTS; downloads from WFS and WCS
- **DatoCMS** as headless CMS; content dumped to static JSON at build/dev time
- **Netlify** hosting + serverless functions (`netlify/functions/api.mjs`)
- **i18n:** `en` and `nl` (`vue-i18n`)

## Architecture

```
DatoCMS (GraphQL)
    ↓  npm run dato  (config/dato/dump-data.mjs)
public/data/{locale}/*.json
    ↓  configRepo / viewer-configs
Vuex (app / data / map)
    ↓
Mapbox map + sidebar UI
```

### Vuex Modules

| Module | Responsibility |
|--------|----------------|
| `app` | Viewer identity: name, config slug, privacy/user agreement, logo, sidebar state |
| `data` | Layer tree from CMS, filters, time extent, CQL filters, opened folders |
| `map` | Active layers, Mapbox layer state, draw mode, map center/zoom |

### Routing

All routes are scoped by viewer config slug: `/:config`, `/:config/download`, `/:config/favourites`, `/:config/filters`.

Valid config slugs come from `public/data/{locale}/available-configs-viewers.json` (generated from DatoCMS menus). Router falls back to the first valid config if slug is invalid. Active layer IDs are synced to the `?layers=` query param.

## Key Directories

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/App.vue` | Root shell: map, sidebar, dialogs, tour, time slider |
| `src/views/` | Route views: Layers, Download, Favourites, Filters |
| `src/components/` | UI components (LayerChooser, MapboxLegend, etc.) |
| `src/lib/` | Layer builders, capabilities parsing, helpers — **core map logic** |
| `src/repo/` | Data access (`configRepo.js`, `metaRepo.js`) |
| `src/store/modules/` | Vuex modules |
| `config/dato/` | DatoCMS dump scripts and GraphQL queries |
| `public/data/` | Generated static JSON (do not hand-edit; regenerate via `npm run dato`) |
