| `scripts/dato/` | Migration create/apply scripts |
| `netlify/functions/` | API proxy to external data services |

## OGC Services and Request Flow

OGC-based map viewer and downloader: WMS/WMTS for map display, WFS/WCS for data download.

### Supported services

| Context | Services | Detection |
|---------|----------|-----------|
| Map display | WMS, WMTS | `src/lib/check-map-service-type.js` — `wmts` in URL pathname, else WMS |
| Data download | WFS, WCS | `src/lib/get-capabilities.js` — probes both via `GetCapabilities`, picks type by layer match |

### User actions → OGC calls

| User action | OGC call | Response |
|-------------|----------|----------|
| Select map layer | WMS/WMTS `GetCapabilities` | Bbox, version, dimensions, formats |
| View layer on map | WMS `GetMap` or WMTS `GetTile` | Map tiles |
| Open Download | WFS/WCS `GetCapabilities` | Supported output formats |
| Configure filters (WFS) | WFS `DescribeFeatureType` | Filterable attributes |
| Download (WFS) | WFS `GetFeature` | Vector dataset |
| Download (WCS) | WCS `GetCoverage` | Raster coverage |

`DescribeCoverage` is not implemented; WCS downloads use `GetCapabilities` + `GetCoverage`.

### Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A[User selects map layer] --> B[WMS/WMTS GetCapabilities]
  B --> C[User views layer on map]
  C --> D[WMS GetMap or WMTS GetTile]
  D --> E[User opens Download]
  E --> F[WFS/WCS GetCapabilities]
  F --> G{Data service type}
  G -->|WFS| H[DescribeFeatureType]
  H --> I[GetFeature]
  G -->|WCS| J[GetCoverage]
```

### OGC-related code

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/lib/get-capabilities.js` | WMS/WMTS/WFS/WCS `GetCapabilities` parsing and service-type detection |
| `src/lib/build-mapbox-layer.js` | Dispatches to `build-wms-layer.js` or `build-wmts-layer.js` |
| `src/lib/get-feature.js` | WFS `GetFeature` URL building |
| `src/lib/wfs-filter-helpers.js` | WFS `DescribeFeatureType` and filter attributes |
| `src/lib/download-helpers.js` | Download URL assembly |
| `src/views/DownloadGeoserver.vue` | Download UI and format/filter resolution |
| `src/components/MapComponents/MapLayer.js` | Renders Mapbox raster layers |

Map layers require `id`, `name`, `url`, and `layer` (layer name).

## Multi-Instance Deployment

Three DatoCMS/Netlify instances in `config/dato/instances.js`:

- `openearth-rws-viewer` (primary RWS viewer)
- `openearth-data-viewer`
- `nl2120`

Set `DATO_INSTANCE_CURRENT` in `.env` to select which instance to dump from. GitHub Actions run Dato migrations and deploy per instance on push/PR.

## Development

```sh
npm install --legacy-peer-deps
cp .env.example .env   # set VUE_APP_MAPBOX_TOKEN, DATO_API_KEY_*, etc.
npm run dato            # get latest information from data
npm run serve           # runs in development
```

- `npm run lint` — ESLint + Stylelint
- `npm run migrations:create` — new DatoCMS migration

## Conventions

- Use existing patterns: Options API in `.vue` files, Ramda for immutable helpers, `~/` alias for `src/`
- Layer/tree helpers live in `src/lib/layer-helpers.js`; don't duplicate flatten/filter logic in components
- Viewer config is locale-specific; always pass `locale` when loading CMS data
- Prefer extending existing layer builders over adding new map integration paths
- SCSS lives in `src/components/AppCore/`; component-scoped styles use Vuetify patterns
- `patch-package` runs on postinstall — check `patches/` before upgrading deps

## Environment Variables (`.env.example`)

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `DATO_INSTANCE_CURRENT` | Which CMS instance to use |
| `DATO_API_KEY_*` | Per-instance DatoCMS API keys |
| `VUE_APP_MAPBOX_TOKEN` | Mapbox access token |
| `VUE_APP_API_ENDPOINT` | External API base URL |
| `VUE_APP_PIWIK_CONTAINER_ID` | Analytics |
| `NODE_OPTIONS=--openssl-legacy-provider` | Required for webpack 4 / Node 17+ |
